* Pass chains

Phase 4 (NOTES.md #P1). A position with no rows is off-system: its call is chosen
by natural inference, and so is every later call of the partnership, because our
own pass is a trie edge only where some row names it. Where this file's answer is
"pass from now on" -- we defend quietly while the opponents bid on, or the
partnership has reached its contract -- the passes are written out: our pass, then
the opponents' next call as the `(any)` wildcard (any call, their pass included),
then our next pass, several rounds deep. The chain's passes carry no requirement
("any hand"). A chain pass pasted into a table is the lowest-ranked call there, so
under the phase-4 policy it is chosen exactly when no other listed call applies,
like the implicit pass it replaces, but the auction stays on the system for the
calls that follow.

`pass-chain` starts with our pass (paste it into a table); `after-chain` starts
with the opponents' call (paste it under a row whose call ends our bidding).

#CUT pass-chain
P = {prio:-100} any hand
  (any)
    P = any hand
      (any)
        P = any hand
          (any)
            P = any hand
              (any)
                P = any hand
                  (any)
                    P = any hand
#ENDCUT

#CUT after-chain
(any)
  P = any hand
    (any)
      P = any hand
        (any)
          P = any hand
            (any)
              P = any hand
                (any)
                  P = any hand
                    (any)
                      P = any hand
#ENDCUT
